{"architectures":["arm","arm64","x64","x86"],"id":"WinDirStat.WinDirStat","latestVersion":"2.9.3","media":{"icons":[],"screenshots":[]},"package":{"description":"WinDirStat is a disk usage statistics viewer and cleanup tool for various versions of Microsoft Windows.","license":"GPL-3.0","licenseUrl":"https://github.com/windirstat/windirstat/blob/HEAD/LICENSE.md","locale":"en-US","localizations":{"en-US":{"description":"WinDirStat is a disk usage statistics viewer and cleanup tool for various versions of Microsoft Windows.","license":"GPL-3.0","licenseUrl":"https://github.com/windirstat/windirstat/blob/HEAD/LICENSE.md","locale":"en-US","longDescription":"WinDirStat (Windows Directory Statistics) is a disk usage statistics viewer and cleanup tool for Windows. On start up, WinDirStat reads the whole directory tree once and then presents it in three useful views:\n- The directory list, which resembles the tree view of the Windows Explorer but is sorted by file/subtree size,\n- The treemap, which shows the whole contents of the directory tree straight away,\n- The extension list, which serves as a legend and shows statistics about the file types.","moniker":"windirstat","name":"WinDirStat","packageUrl":"https://github.com/windirstat/windirstat/releases/","publisher":"The WinDirStat Team","publisherUrl":"https://windirstat.net/","releaseNotesUrl":"https://github.com/windirstat/windirstat/blob/master/CHANGELOG.md#windirstat-2.9.3","tags":["cleanup","disk-space-analyzer","disk-usage-analyzer","duplicate-detection","treemap","treemaps","windows"]}},"longDescription":"WinDirStat (Windows Directory Statistics) is a disk usage statistics viewer and cleanup tool for Windows. On start up, WinDirStat reads the whole directory tree once and then presents it in three useful views:\n- The directory list, which resembles the tree view of the Windows Explorer but is sorted by file/subtree size,\n- The treemap, which shows the whole contents of the directory tree straight away,\n- The e